  "findings": "Basal rosette, smaller cauline leaves, tall one-sided dense tubular raceme. Generic giant leaves and four tiny bells rejected. Dedicated digitalis staged. Current seeds 1, 4 and 7 and every panel in the 36-seed contact sheet were visually inspected. Basal rosettes have bounded leaf lengths, smaller cauline leaves and tall one-sided pink racemes. The 0.78\u20131.60 m forms retain varied height and lean. Individual tubular cavities and spotting remain unresolved; low connecting geometry requires soil embedding. Accepted as a coarse stylized spring source at 25 mm; user endorsement remains separate.",
